WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.440
- [Interviewer] All right Ray, Ray,

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.460
where are you from originally,
where'd you grow up?

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.120
- [Ray] Oakland.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.870
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your family,

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.660
you grew up with both your parents?

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.423
- Yeah, for a little while.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.533
Um, as a child,

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.800
they would um, they would get drunk.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.970
It was my father and he had a little job,

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.350
but when he'd get drunk,

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.053
he would always beat
my mother up, you know,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.217
argue with her and do
all kind of stuff to her,

00:00:44.308 --> 00:00:46.433
and me and my brother,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.800
we used to get upset and then
she would take it out on us,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.403
trying to get back at him.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:57.153
And,

00:00:59.266 --> 00:01:00.966
it was terrible and then sometimes

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.950
my brother got molested one time

00:01:06.706 --> 00:01:10.197
and then he end up
getting killed behind it.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.930
'Cause my father and mother were fighting

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.110
and he ran out in the
street and got hit by a car.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.880
- [Interviewer] Oh my God, what age?

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.380
- He was like three years old.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.450
Yeah, so I end up

00:01:31.795 --> 00:01:36.190
hurting this dude that ran
over my little brother.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:39.363
Later on I end up shooting him.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:47.060
Nobody really knows I did
it, but I got my revenge.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.810
And it bothers me a lot of times

00:01:53.096 --> 00:01:56.400
to think about it, that I did it.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.923
I kind of regret it, but
he killed my brother,

00:02:00.832 --> 00:02:02.144
he ran over him in the car.

00:02:02.144 --> 00:02:03.113
- [Interviewer] I mean did--

00:02:03.113 --> 00:02:03.946
- My little brother, yeah.

00:02:03.946 --> 00:02:05.283
- [Interviewer] On purpose or?

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:08.810
Or it was just an accident?

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.513
- Accident probably, most likely.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.850
But I just feel like I'm regretful

00:02:16.342 --> 00:02:18.543
'cause I think it was an accident.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:20.853
But I,

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:22.943
I still did it.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:28.043
I feel guilty about it a lot of times.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.202
You know, I hear, "You're going to Hell,

00:02:31.202 --> 00:02:33.320
"you're going to Hell, it's murder."

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.053
Stuff like that, voices,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.950
from time to time and it troubles me, so,

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.260
I will end up going to

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.930
the right hospital for it

00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:49.398
just so they can give me medications.

00:02:49.398 --> 00:02:53.580
I could never tell 'em what I did

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.850
and what was really bothering
me, the voices that I heard.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.080
I found out later that my dad,

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.877
he was in a mental hospital too.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.140
My mother, she was from Texas,

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.510
she was a good woman

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.040
'til he started, really

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:24.056
making her drink and he used
to make a mess of my mother

00:03:24.056 --> 00:03:26.113
(muttering) and I used to hate him.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.180
He put his car on the flat,

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.313
do stuff like that.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.643
Well she used to take it out on us.

00:03:35.503 --> 00:03:38.593
She just made me get in
the box when I was little,

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.152
mad at him, trying to take it out on him.

00:03:42.152 --> 00:03:45.330
"You're just like him,"
make me get in the box.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.743
I'd stay in there for hours.

00:03:48.442 --> 00:03:51.287
I'd say, "Mama, please don't
make me get in the box,

00:03:51.287 --> 00:03:53.087
"please don't put me in a box."

00:03:55.183 --> 00:03:56.333
Make me stay in the box

00:03:57.812 --> 00:03:59.312
when I was little.

00:04:01.743 --> 00:04:03.576
It all because of him.

00:04:06.853 --> 00:04:09.993
I never had a car in my life.

00:04:12.931 --> 00:04:17.683
I had an under-the-table job before,

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.370
but because of my conditions,

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:26.040
it's hard for me to kinda
deal with people like that

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.740
'cause I end up getting upset and

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.883
I go back into my old way of thinking.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.673
Murder,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.043
I did it once and I'd do it again.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.760
You know, I'll kill you.

00:04:45.012 --> 00:04:46.433
But um, yeah.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:49.373
So now I'm older now.

00:04:51.783 --> 00:04:54.763
I'm still dealing with them, I'm homeless.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.183
I stay away from all the
people that I used to know.

00:05:01.682 --> 00:05:05.210
Most of those have fallen
off and died and shot,

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:10.210
whatever, sick, gone away, jail, prison.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.740
I'm still here, but my life is empty

00:05:19.522 --> 00:05:24.522
and I really don't have a whole
lotta good times in my life.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.943
Lotta suffering.

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.523
Without, uneducated.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.190
I wish I coulda been a
lawyer, doctor or a judge

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.340
or something like that.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:53.783
I miss my mom.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.555
(sighs)

00:06:02.759 --> 00:06:05.509
(crying quietly)

00:06:51.302 --> 00:06:54.885
So now I do stuff to
myself because it has,

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:57.493
mistreat myself.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.353
Wanted to die.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.630
(sighs)

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.200
I don't really have anything in my life.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.160
I think that's the reason why, maybe,

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:25.333
my life has been like that.

00:07:27.907 --> 00:07:29.907
(sighs)

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:38.363
There's a lot of stuff
that happened to my mom.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.380
She died from,

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.363
from dealing with my father,

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.417
beating her and doing stuff to her.

00:07:52.321 --> 00:07:54.404
(crying)

00:08:07.324 --> 00:08:08.157
The way she used to treat me,

00:08:08.157 --> 00:08:11.673
I don't think she loved
me at all. (crying)

00:08:28.723 --> 00:08:29.890
A lot of pain.

00:08:31.092 --> 00:08:33.143
A lot of pain, pain. (crying)

00:08:45.056 --> 00:08:46.223
A lot of pain.

00:08:53.539 --> 00:08:56.125
Oh. (crying)

00:08:56.125 --> 00:09:00.210
I'm trying just to learn
how to deal with (sighs)

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:05.060
deal with it. (crying)

00:09:09.208 --> 00:09:11.291
I hardly have no friends.

00:09:12.762 --> 00:09:14.762
(sighs)

00:09:16.921 --> 00:09:20.260
I can't have friends, I don't
know how to have friends.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:23.313
We end up getting into fights.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:33.380
I had a girlfriend, I had
a girlfriend before, but,

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:34.250
just

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.433
they say I'm too crazy.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:47.833
Too strict, too jealous, whatever.

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:54.040
(sniffs)

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:55.627
- [Interviewer] Do you
have kids of your own?

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:58.703
- I have one kid.

00:09:59.879 --> 00:10:01.820
She took him away.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:04.173
I never (mutters) I saw a picture,

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:06.403
but that was it.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:13.640
She said it was my kid,
but I don't know for sure

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.313
if he was really my kid or not.

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:22.443
Yeah.

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:26.423
Driver's license, I never
had a driver's license.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.160
I wish I could uh,

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.667
have a car before I die.

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.797
I haven't been able to get a car,

00:10:35.797 --> 00:10:37.603
never had a car in my life.

00:10:41.061 --> 00:10:43.644
Never had a house or apartment.

00:10:51.571 --> 00:10:56.463
I feel like, almost like
I'm a handicap or something.

00:11:00.731 --> 00:11:02.731
(sighs)

00:11:04.252 --> 00:11:06.200
(exhales)

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:08.820
- [Interviewer] If there was
one thing about your life

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.890
that you could have changed

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:13.130
to change your path and direction,

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.223
what do you think that might have been?

00:11:15.223 --> 00:11:16.103
That would be?

00:11:18.831 --> 00:11:20.523
- (sighs) Murder.

00:11:26.212 --> 00:11:27.045
Murder.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.500
- [Interviewer] Do you
still carry that with you

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.333
to this day?

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:33.643
- Yep.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:35.493
Yeah.

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:38.143
Yeah.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.573
I think some day somebody'll shoot me.

00:11:44.601 --> 00:11:46.143
That's what this (muttering) paranoid,

00:11:46.143 --> 00:11:47.810
going through so many things,

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.330
I have to take pills and stuff,

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.743
try to get stuff outta my head.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:55.193
- [Interviewer] How did you kill him?

00:11:56.753 --> 00:11:57.586
- Gun.

00:11:59.945 --> 00:12:01.440
- [Interviewer] With a gun?

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.273
- Yep.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.300
- [Interviewer] How old were you?

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:08.133
- I was 13.

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:13.367
13 years old.

00:12:17.063 --> 00:12:18.146
13 years old.

00:12:24.323 --> 00:12:27.823
So I've been living with that, I'm 58 now.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:34.100
So it's really have a
toll on my life, you know,

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.103
my mind and stuff.

00:12:39.337 --> 00:12:44.337
And after dealing with abusive family,

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.253
drunks,

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.073
lack of love,

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:52.593
care,

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.673
barely had clothes,

00:12:57.754 --> 00:12:58.723
shoes.

00:13:01.245 --> 00:13:03.245
(sighs)

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:16.340
I had to hustle, try to
hustle up our own food

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.063
'cause they messed money up.

00:13:28.729 --> 00:13:30.812
(crying)

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:35.053
You have uh.

00:13:47.621 --> 00:13:49.621
(sighs)

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:05.043
So try to,

00:14:10.511 --> 00:14:12.940
(sighs)

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:16.173
try to maybe get some counseling.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.213
I tired before,

00:14:20.141 --> 00:14:22.193
maybe, I don't know.

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.183
I take medications.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:35.080
Often time I think about

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:38.670
committing suicide.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:39.700
I'm suicidal

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.300
because of all of that.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.263
I was molested as a child.

00:14:58.932 --> 00:15:00.932
(sighs)

00:15:04.912 --> 00:15:06.993
- [Interviewer] Who molested you?

00:15:06.993 --> 00:15:07.826
- My dad.

00:15:28.063 --> 00:15:30.132
(sighs)

00:15:30.132 --> 00:15:32.215
(crying)

00:15:56.866 --> 00:16:01.703
Since I was, this is how my life is now.

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:04.283
I'm homeless.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:09.143
I have a little tent that
I'm trying to sleep in.

00:16:12.394 --> 00:16:14.394
(sighs)

00:16:24.673 --> 00:16:29.673
I have no real friends. (sighs)

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.270
- [Interviewer] Do you use
drugs to help you deal with

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:39.020
any of the stuff you went through?

00:16:40.036 --> 00:16:42.683
- [Ray] (sighs) Alcohol,

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.323
drugs sometime,

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:48.433
pills,

00:16:49.856 --> 00:16:52.090
to sedate myself from the voices.

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:08.459
Still hear my dad's voice
hollering at my mother

00:17:08.459 --> 00:17:11.803
and her hollering at me
and putting me in a box.

00:17:14.201 --> 00:17:15.063
It's a lot of stuff,

00:17:16.831 --> 00:17:18.081
a lot of stuff.

00:17:19.931 --> 00:17:21.040
It's been so bad

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:25.583
for me.

00:17:31.947 --> 00:17:35.347
(sighs) I think one day of,

00:17:35.347 --> 00:17:36.220
that's the thing,

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.753
maybe I'll find a million
dollars or something.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:44.560
(sighs) And buy a house and a car

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.393
and maybe get married.

00:17:58.676 --> 00:18:01.440
(wheezing)

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:02.923
- [Interviewer] Have
you been in love before?

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.163
- Yeah.

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:07.843
She left me.

00:18:15.945 --> 00:18:18.580
We was together for three years and

00:18:18.580 --> 00:18:19.793
finally she left.

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:24.013
She met somebody else.

00:18:28.014 --> 00:18:29.414
I couldn't take care of her.

00:18:43.148 --> 00:18:43.981
So,

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:56.003
(crying)

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.387
Parts of my life like this

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:15.320
other people (mutters)

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:19.360
they have good lives.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:23.850
They have good family.

00:19:26.805 --> 00:19:28.805
(sighs)

00:20:00.396 --> 00:20:03.733
I was thinking about
committing suicide lately,

00:20:03.733 --> 00:20:05.323
it's been bothering me.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.233
'Cause of the pain in my life.

00:20:27.718 --> 00:20:29.963
(muttering) I love their kids.

00:20:31.026 --> 00:20:33.035
It's a mystery to 'em like that.

00:20:33.035 --> 00:20:33.952
Some other,

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:44.473
makes me violent.

00:20:52.504 --> 00:20:54.504
(sighs)

00:21:05.563 --> 00:21:07.813
(wheezing)

00:21:12.614 --> 00:21:14.697
(crying)

00:21:32.251 --> 00:21:33.501
I apologize for

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.653
for tears, it's crying stuff.

00:21:43.997 --> 00:21:46.080
(crying)

00:21:53.318 --> 00:21:55.735
I don't know what I would do,

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:04.200
(sighs)

00:22:09.044 --> 00:22:11.044
(sighs)

00:22:14.935 --> 00:22:15.837
(exhales)

00:22:15.837 --> 00:22:18.343
but I try really hard
though, to deal with it.

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:29.743
Nobody really cares.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:33.843
Wish I coulda shared a
great story with you,

00:22:35.051 --> 00:22:37.013
but that's been my life.

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:46.113
That's been my life.

00:22:49.420 --> 00:22:50.253
- [Interviewer] All right, Ray,

00:22:50.253 --> 00:22:52.493
well thank you for coming
in and sharing your story.

00:22:57.210 --> 00:22:58.860
- Thank you for letting me share.

00:23:00.233 --> 00:23:02.233
(sighs)

00:23:04.642 --> 00:23:06.809
(crying)

